  "text": "Dubai residential activity accelerated in the four weeks to 9 November 2026. Registered sales reached 13,717 units, a 34.5% increase from the previous four-week period. Total transaction value rose 47.4% to AED 40.78bn. Mortgage registrations were separate from sales and totaled 5,775 during the same window.\n\nMedian residential pricing climbed 4.6% to AED 1,741 per square foot. Off-plan transactions accounted for 57.6% of the volume. The rental market recorded 92,075 Ejari contracts with a 51.8% renewal share. The median annual residential rent stood at AED 69,479.\n\nTwelve-week price momentum shows Al Yufrah 1 leading with a 43.8% increase in median price per square foot. Dubai Industrial City followed at 13.6% and Dubai Production City at 8.3%. Conversely, Jumeirah Lakes Towers and Palm Jumeirah cooled by 14.6% and 14.3% respectively. Zaabeel First offers the highest estimated gross yield at 9.0% for flats, while International City Phase 1 follows at 8.6%.\n\nInvestors should monitor the 941 sales flagged as anomalies in the last 60 days. These transactions deviated more than 35% from comparable medians. Figures are derived from registered DLD data and Ejari contracts. Benchmarks exclude bulk deals, partial shares, portfolio blocks, mortgages, gifts, and statistical outliers.",
